  "attribution": "International Personality Item Pool (IPIP), 50-item Big Five Factor Markers. These five scales were developed to measure the Big-Five factor markers reported in Goldberg, L. R. (1992). The development of markers for the Big-Five factor structure. Psychological Assessment, 4, 26–42.",
  "rightsSummary": "Official IPIP items, scales and inventories are public domain for any purpose, commercial or non-commercial. All 50 English items, the sample item order, five response anchors and ten-item factor keys are preserved. Administration instructions are expressly suggestions, not standardized requirements. The sample sentence promising absolute confidence is deliberately omitted: Kairos must explain actual privacy and storage separately and must not imply an absolute security guarantee. No other sample response instruction is changed. Source factor/sign annotations are scoring metadata, not respondent-facing item text.",
